# DichThuat Core Rules

Read `CONTEXT.md` at project start for terminology and workflow.

## Language Pair

- Source: Chinese (Traditional preferred; note if Simplified)
- Target: Vietnamese (formal Buddhist register)

## Output Location

- Write translations only under `web/data/translations/`, mirroring `web/data/sources/` paths (logical paths: `translations/...`, `sources/...`)
- Sources may be added via web **Upload** or agent segmentation into `web/data/sources/`
- Source bodies (`.zh.md`): ASCII punctuation only — normalize Chinese marks on import/edit (full table in `chinese-source` rule / `segment-source` skill)
- Never overwrite sources except when fixing OCR or segmentation errors (note in commit/message)

## Terminology

- Check `web/data/glossary/terms.yaml` before translating; add new terms (`hv` + `vi`) before first use
- One Chinese term → one `hv` and one `vi` equivalent per series
- **`.hv.md` (Hán-Việt):** use glossary `hv` column only — never `vi` when they differ
- **`.vi.md` (thuần Việt):** use glossary `vi` column only — never `hv` when they differ
- Sanskrit/Pali & transliterated names: no hyphens; write each syllable as a separate Title Case word (e.g. Niết Bàn, Bồ Tát, Bát Nhã Ba La Mật, A Nan)

## Translation Output Format (plain text)

Translation files (`.hv.md`, `.vi.md`) are **plain text bodies** — not structured Markdown.

- **One source line → one translation line** (same line count as source body)
- **One source paragraph → one translation paragraph** on the matching line
- **Do not add** `#` / `##` headings, editorial subsections, or intro blocks not in the source
- **Do not split** one source paragraph into multiple output paragraphs
- **Do not merge** multiple source paragraphs into one output line
- Preserve blank lines exactly where the source has them
- **No duplicate blank lines**: collapse consecutive empty lines to match the source (agents sometimes insert an extra blank line — remove it before save)
- Preserve verse line breaks and enumeration order (一、二、三…)
- Uncertain readings: inline `[?]`; full notes go in `notes/`, not in the translation file
- Metadata (`status`, `revision`, glossary refs): log in `notes/`, not in translation files

## Quality Bar

- Mark uncertain readings: `[?]`; explain in `notes/`
- Do not add commentary in translation files unless user requests 註解
- Flag doctrinal ambiguity rather than guessing

## Session Start

When user names a chapter, read: source file → relevant glossary entries → `docs/style-guide.md` if needed.
